[metadata]
Name:Rules pilot 243 - The trigger outlives its source
Goal:Survive
Turns:1
Difficulty:Hard
Description:You control Thing in the Ice with two ice counters on it, Grizzly Bears and six Islands, and have Divination and Snakeform in hand. End the turn with Awoken Horror and Grizzly Bears on your battlefield.
Rule:rulesguru-6c7ca7e941f641bd | A triggered ability on the stack exists independently of its source (CR 113.7a): Thing in the Ice that lost its abilities still loses its last ice counter and transforms, but it is the same object, so Snakeform's ability loss persists (CR 712.18) and Awoken Horror's transform trigger does not exist: cast Divination, then Snakeform Thing in the Ice in response to its trigger
